#   5. after Zenodo has minted the DOI, add the concept DOI under identifiers.
# Do not add a DOI before Zenodo has issued it.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TODSphere, please cite the software and the accompanying article."
type: software
title: "TODSphere: open-data screening of transit-oriented development with the Node–Place–People–Ecology (NPPE) framework"
version: "2.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-28"
authors:
  - family-names: Varma
    given-names: D. Sai Kiran
    affiliation: "Shiv Nadar Institution of Eminence, Delhi NCR, India"
  - family-names: Rankavat
    given-names: Shalini
    # affiliation: not recorded in the repository; add it before release
repository-code: "https://github.com/OWNER/todsphere"
license: NOASSERTION
keywords:
  - transit-oriented development
  - node-place model
  - NPPE
  - OpenStreetMap
  - composite indicators
  - planning support system
  - air quality
abstract: >-
  TODSphere is a browser-based, zero-installation tool that computes seven open-data indicators of
  transit-oriented development readiness (transit accessibility, built density, land-use diversity,
  walkability, amenity accessibility, green space and near-road air quality) from OpenStreetMap and CAMS,
  aggregates them into the Node, Place, People and Ecology dimensions, and reports compensatory and
  non-compensatory composites, a balance ratio and the limiting dimension, with corridor ranking and
  robustness analysis. Version 2.1.0 implements methodology NPPE-7 v1.0.0 and reproduces the results of
  the accompanying manuscript.
